  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAtr">II Atr</ref> 4</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">[Be ðon ðe mon on scip bereafod sy.] [Ld] Gyf man beo æt his æhtan bereafod, ⁊ he wite of hwilcum scipe, agyfe steoresman ða æhta oððon gange feowra sum tó ⁊ oðsace—⁊ beo him sylf fifta—þæt he hit ariht name, swa hit ær geforword wæs.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">If anyone has been robbed of this goods and he knows the ship by which it has been done, the captain shall restore the goods or shall go with four compurgators—himself making one—and deny [the charge, proving] that he was justified in taking them, according to the terms laid down above.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Si homo sit de pecunia sua robatus et sciat, in qua naui, reddat steoresman (id est gubernator) pecuniam illam uel cum quatuor iuret—et idem sit quintis—, quod per rectitudinem cepit, sicut antea prelocutum erit.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
